THE LORD OF THE CAGES

One Cage to rule them all. One Cage to find them. One Cage to bring them all and absolutely lose his fucking mind.

The movie opens on a peaceful green hillside.

Tiny houses. Sheep. Wind through the grass.

Then Nicolas Cage narrates:

“There were once twenty Rings of Power.”

Pause.

“Unfortunately, I bought nineteen of them on eBay.”

Cut to Hobbiton.

Every hobbit is Nicolas Cage.

Not digitally altered. Just full-size Nicolas Cage wearing increasingly disrespectful amounts of forced perspective.

Frodo Cage is sitting outside smoking a pipe.

Sam Cage walks up.

“Mr. Cage.”

Frodo:

“Samwise Cage.”

Sam:

“You are also Cage.”

Frodo:

“Don’t make this about blood.”

Then Gandalf Cage arrives on a cart.

Beard down to his knees.

He is driving way too fast.

Children-Cage chase him screaming.

Gandalf Cage throws fireworks into the crowd with the confidence of a man distributing tactical ordnance.

“THEY’RE SAFE.”

One explodes into the shape of Nicolas Cage’s face.

Everybody applauds.

One tiny hobbit Cage whispers:

“He came back.”

Nobody knows what that means.

⸻

At Bilbo Cage’s birthday party, Bilbo Cage gives the speech.

“My dear Cages…”

Every single person in the crowd looks up.

“…You know half of me half as well as I deserve—”

Gandalf leans toward Frodo.

“He rehearsed this.”

Bilbo Cage suddenly puts on the Ring.

Vanishes.

Crowd gasps.

Except Gandalf Cage.

He just stares at the empty spot and whispers:

“Classic.”

⸻

Later, Gandalf throws the Ring into the fireplace.

Frodo reaches for it.

Gandalf slaps his hand.

“HOT.”

“You told me to pick it up!”

“AFTER.”

They wait.

Frodo eventually grabs it.

Letters appear.

But instead of Elvish, they spell:

NICOLAS WAS HERE

Frodo:

“…What the fuck?”

Gandalf slowly sits down.

“I was afraid of this.”

“Of what?”

Gandalf leans in.

“That Ring does not belong to Sauron.”

Lightning outside.

“It belongs to Nicolas Cage.”

Frodo:

“Which one?”

Gandalf looks devastated.

“Exactly.”

⸻

CUT TO:

MORDOR

A giant flaming eye atop Barad-dûr.

Except the eye is Nicolas Cage’s face.

Just one enormous Cage eyeball rotating in the sky.

Sauron Cage speaks telepathically:

“WHERE IS MY JEWELRY?”

Orc Cage:

“We’re searching, my lord.”

Sauron Cage:

“I CAN SEE EVERYTHING.”

Orc Cage:

“Then why are we searching?”

Long silence.

Sauron Cage:

“…INSUBORDINATION.”

Orc Cage gets launched off tower.

Another Orc Cage steps forward.

“You just killed the logistics officer.”

Sauron:

“PROMOTE SOMEBODY.”

⸻

Meanwhile Frodo Cage and Sam Cage are walking.

Sam is carrying seventeen pans.

Frodo:

“Why did you bring all that?”

Sam:

“Meal prep.”

“We are crossing Middle-earth.”

“You’ll thank me at second breakfast.”

A third voice from a bush:

“What about third breakfast?”

Both freeze.

Out crawls Gollum Cage.

Bald.

Filthy.

Still somehow wearing a snakeskin jacket.

He sees the Ring.

His eyes widen.

“MY PRECIOUSSSSS.”

Then immediately switches demeanor.

“No, sorry. That was weird.”

Two seconds later:

“GIVE IT TO ME.”

Sam hits him with a frying pan.

Gollum:

“OW.”

Then, from inside Gollum’s own head, Sméagol Cage begins arguing.

Gollum:

“We should kill them.”

Sméagol:

“We should help them.”

Gollum:

“We should steal the Ring.”

Sméagol:

“We should start a podcast.”

Frodo:

“What are you doing?”

Gollum:

“BUILDING A BRAND.”

⸻

Elsewhere, the Fellowship forms.

Aragorn Cage enters first.

Unshaven. Cloak. Sword.

He looks like Cage wandered out of a Renaissance fair after losing a custody dispute with destiny.

Legolas Cage is blond.

Far too blond.

He fires three arrows simultaneously.

All three hit the same tree.

Legolas:

“Warning shots.”

Gimli Cage is four feet tall and approximately 90% beard.

He points at Legolas.

“Nobody tosses a Cage.”

Legolas:

“I wasn’t going to.”

Gimli:

“I KNOW WHAT YOU WERE THINKING.”

Boromir Cage walks in holding a shield and already looking like he is about to make one absolutely terrible decision.

He sees the Ring.

“We could use it.”

Everyone:

“NO.”

Boromir:

“I hadn’t finished.”

Aragorn:

“You were done.”

Then the door opens.

Elrond Cage enters wearing the most aggressive elf eyebrows ever committed to cinema.

He says:

“The Ring must be destroyed.”

Everyone looks at Frodo.

Frodo:

“Why me?”

Every other Cage looks away.

Frodo:

“Seriously?”

Gandalf Cage coughs.

“You have protagonist cheekbones.”

⸻

They enter Moria.

Dark.

Silent.

Gimli Cage shouts:

“MY COUSIN CAGE WILL GIVE US A ROYAL WELCOME.”

They find skeletons everywhere.

Gimli slowly removes helmet.

“Cage…”

One skeleton has a little name tag:

HELLO, MY NAME IS CAGE

Gimli:

“…fuck.”

Then drums begin.

Boom.

Boom.

Boom.

Pippin Cage whispers:

“What is that?”

Gandalf Cage:

“A cave troll.”

Merry Cage:

“How do you know?”

Gandalf:

“I’ve been in movies.”

A troll bursts through the door.

It is also Nicolas Cage.

Huge.

Gray.

Wearing one enormous earring for no reason.

Troll Cage:

“RRRAAAAAAGH.”

Regular Cages:

“NICOLAS?”

Troll stops.

Looks around.

“…Dad?”

Nobody knows who he is addressing.

Fight resumes immediately.

⸻

Then comes the bridge.

Gandalf Cage faces Balrog Cage.

Balrog Cage is twenty feet tall, on fire, and has the exact same Nicolas Cage facial expression as everyone else.

Gandalf plants his staff.

“YOU SHALL NOT—”

Balrog Cage interrupts.

“DON’T YOU FUCKING DO IT.”

Gandalf:

“DO WHAT?”

“You know.”

“I HAVE TO.”

“IT’S A MEME NOW.”

“I SAID IT FIRST.”

“No you didn’t!”

Gandalf turns to Fellowship.

“RUN.”

Then, louder:

“YOU SHALL NOT—”

The bridge collapses before he finishes.

Gandalf falls.

While falling:

“PASS—aaaaaaaahhhhhh.”

Aragorn Cage watches.

“…He still got it.”

⸻

Later, Frodo and Sam reach Mount Doom.

Exhausted.

Dirty.

Emotionally obliterated.

Frodo holds the Ring over the lava.

Sam Cage:

“Do it.”

Frodo stares.

“No.”

Sam:

“What?”

Frodo Cage slowly turns.

His eyes are insane.

“The Ring is mine.”

Then from above:

“NEGATIVE.”

Everybody looks up.

A giant eagle descends.

It has Nicolas Cage’s face.

Eagle Cage.

Sam:

“WHERE THE FUCK HAVE YOU BEEN?”

Eagle Cage:

“TRAFFIC.”

Frodo:

“You could’ve flown us here?”

Eagle Cage:

“…That is not relevant.”

Then Gollum Cage tackles Frodo.

They wrestle.

Ring flies into the air.

Everybody screams.

At the exact same moment, from behind a rock, The Quarter rolls into frame.

Little Nick, dressed as Tom Bombadil for no explained reason, whispers:

“Third option.”

The Ring lands upright on the Quarter.

Does not fall.

Lava stops moving.

Mount Doom goes silent.

Then the Ring speaks.

In Nicolas Cage’s voice.

“I don’t want to be destroyed.”

Everyone:

“WHAT?”

The Ring:

“I’ve been under tremendous pressure.”

Sam:

“You’re jewelry.”

Ring:

“THAT DOES NOT NEGATE MY INTERIORITY.”

Gollum Cage starts crying.

“I knew you understood me.”

⸻

Final confrontation.

Sauron Cage manifests physically.

Nine feet tall.

Black armor.

Cape.

Absolutely gorgeous hair flowing somehow despite being inside a volcano.

He points at Frodo.

“GIVE ME THE RING.”

Frodo:

“No.”

Sauron:

“WHY?”

Frodo:

“Because I’ve learned something.”

Sam:

“Oh God.”

Frodo:

“This was never about power.”

Sauron:

“What?”

“It was about…”

He looks around at all the other Nicolas Cages.

“…family.”

Every Cage groans.

Gimli Cage:

“Fuck me.”

Aragorn Cage:

“He went there.”

Sauron Cage starts crying.

“Dad?”

Everyone:

“WHO ARE YOU CALLING DAD?”

Mount Doom erupts.

⸻

Cut to black.

Then peaceful music.

The Shire is restored.

All is well.

Frodo Cage sits down to finish his memoir.

Title:

THERE AND BACK AGAIN AND ALSO SOME OTHER SHIT

Sam Cage leans over.

“You gonna mention me?”

Frodo:

“Depends.”

“On?”

“How you behave in the sequel.”

Camera pans upward.

Far away, beyond the mountains, an enormous figure rises.

Twenty stories tall.

Tan trench coat.

Beard made of clouds.

BIGGER GANDALF CAGE.

He looks down at Middle-earth.

“YOU FOOLS.”

Little Nick, from somewhere offscreen:

“Oh, come the fuck on.”

THE LORD OF THE CAGES II: THE TWO NICOLASES

One does not simply walk into Mordor.

Nicolas Cage absolutely fucking does.